// * JSON strings (starting with `[` or `{`) are parsed as JSON objects/arrays
// * Non-convertible strings remain strings
// * The provider merges these keys into the `litellmParams` payload sent to the API.
// * Note: the remote API may not echo back all custom parameters; this provider preserves `additionalLitellmParams` in state when present in configuration.
//
// **`additionalDropParams`**
// * Give it a JSON array string, such as `jsonencode(["store"])`. The provider sends the list to the proxy as the deployment's `additionalDropParams`, and the proxy applies it the same as `additionalDropParams` in a `modelList` entry. `pulumi preview` fails on any other value, an empty value, or an entry that is not a name, and `null` entries are skipped
// * Other keys on the resource, such as `vertexLocation`, are sent unchanged
// * When the configuration sets the list, refresh reads the stored list back from the proxy, so a list changed outside Terraform shows up as drift. A model whose configuration has no list keeps a list set outside Terraform out of the plan, but the proxy clears it on the next update
// * When the proxy has no stored list, as on a model an older provider created, the next plan shows the list and every listed key the configuration sets as changes, since the next apply writes them
//
// Example showing booleans, integers, floats, strings, JSON, and dropped request parameters:
//
// ```go
// package main
//
// import (
//
//	"github.com/primait/pulumi-litellm/sdk/go/litellm"
//	"github.com/pulumi/pulumi/sdk/v3/go/pulumi"
//
// )
